{
  "key": "past_tense",
  "concept_slug": "past_tense",
  "grounding_mode": "fallback_no_wiki",
  "title": "The Past Tense (Preteritum)",
  "cefr_level": "A2",
  "goal": "Form and use the Norwegian preteritum (simple past) of regular and common irregular verbs, and choose it when the time of an action is known.",
  "objectives": [
    {
      "id": "o1",
      "statement": "Learn past_tense",
      "bloom_targets": [
        "remember",
        "apply"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "elements": [
    {
      "element_kind": "section",
      "id": "s1",
      "role": "orient",
      "objective_ids": [
        "o1"
      ],
      "title": "What the past tense is for",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "When you talk about something that happened and finished at a known time in the past, Norwegian uses the "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "preteritum",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": " — the simple past tense (like English \"walked\", \"ate\"). In this lesson you'll learn how to build it for regular verbs, for common irregular verbs, and for the modal verbs you already know."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "I går spiste vi middag klokka fem."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Yesterday we ate dinner at five."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "element_kind": "section",
      "id": "s2",
      "role": "model",
      "objective_ids": [
        "o1"
      ],
      "title": "Regular verbs: the main Bokmål endings",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Most Norwegian verbs are regular (\"weak\"): you keep the stem and add one of the main written Bokmål endings — "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "-et, -te, -de, -dde",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": ". The stem is usually the infinitive minus its final "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "-e",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": " (snakke → snakk-), and for short verbs without a final -e it is the infinitive itself (bo, tro). Many verbs that take -et also have an allowed -a form in Bokmål, but this lesson uses the common -et form."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "table",
          "col_langs": [
            "no",
            "no",
            "no",
            "no"
          ],
          "headers": [
            [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Infinitiv"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Presens"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Preteritum"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Perfektum"
              }
            ]
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "å snakke"
                }
              ],
              [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "snakker"
                }
              ],
              [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "snakket"
                }
              ],
              [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "har snakket"
                }
              ]
            ],
            [
              [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "å spise"
                }
              ],
              [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "spiser"
                }
