    {
      "element_kind": "section",
      "id": "s5",
      "role": "model",
      "objective_ids": [
        "o1"
      ],
      "title": "When to choose the preteritum: time signals",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Use the preteritum when the action belongs to a finished past time — very often words like i går or i fjor make this clear. If you can answer when? with a finished past time, the preteritum is usually right."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "rule",
          "statement": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "With a specific past time — "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "i går",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": " (yesterday), "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "i fjor",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": " (last year), "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "da",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": " (when) — use the preteritum."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Martin jobbet i en bank da han bodde i USA."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Martin worked in a bank when he lived in the USA."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "rule",
          "statement": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "When a time phrase comes first, the verb still comes second (V2): "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "I går spiste vi middag",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": " — not "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "I går vi spiste",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "rule",
          "statement": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "In a subject-first clause, put "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "ikke",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": " right after the finite verb: "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "Jeg gikk ikke på jobb i går",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "rule",
          "statement": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "After a fronted past-time phrase, pronoun subjects normally come before "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "ikke",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": ": "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "I går gikk jeg ikke på jobb",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "You'll have noticed the "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "Perfektum",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": " column (har snakket, har gått). You will learn this form in a separate lesson. It is common when the time is not a finished past time, or when the focus is experience, result, or an unfinished period: "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "Jeg har sett filmen",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": ". Finished past-time expressions like "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "i går",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": " and "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "i fjor",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": " normally take the preteritum: "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "Jeg så filmen i går",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "element_kind": "section",
      "id": "s6",
      "role": "recap",
      "objective_ids": [
        "o1"
      ],
      "title": "Putting it together",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Regular verbs add an ending (snakket, spiste, bodde); common irregular verbs must be learned as forms (gikk, så, var, hadde, gjorde); modals have their own past forms (skulle, ville, kunne). Reach for the preteritum whenever the time of the action is known."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "element_kind": "exercise",
      "id": "ex-match-inf-pret",
      "operation": "match_pairs",
      "objective_id": "o1",
      "bloom_level": "apply",
      "prompt": [
